# Required nullary control; no one-argument shim is an acceptable substitute.
# wrap's header declares a callable of no formals: w() passes none. The held
# call takes the arguments of its header at any count, zero included.
fn: get () int
return: 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        fn: get
    return: S\get()
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
w: wrap 5
int: result w()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
